            "review_title": "Review at Cherry Kitchen",
            "review_text": "Andrew S\nVancouver, British Columbia, Canada3 contributions\n0\nWorst service in Ho Chi Minh\nFeb 2016 • Couples\nIn nearly one month in Ho Chi Minh, this was easily both the worst food and worst service I have received so far. I went to Cherry Kitchen on February 20th for a late night snack, ordering a beef shwarma. What came wasn't anything resembling anything remotely resembling a shwarma--it was so drowned in ketchup that I literally could taste nothing else. No one asked me what I'd like on this, and no shwarma anywhere I've ever eaten has been done in this way. \n\nWhen I asked it to be served instead without ketchup, my meal was discarded, and I was told if I wanted it fixed, I was charged for a second order(!)\n\nWhen I mentioned I had been a customer for over a week, I was informed that they \"couldn't afford to replace it\" (at 40,000 Dong.)\n\nI've never seen such customer service so disregarded in my life. Terrible, awful, unfriendly service.\nRead more\nWritten February 20, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
