            "review_text": "Constantine_Dudnick\nMirissa, Sri Lanka10 contributions\n0\nCheap and authentic indian food\nJan 2016 • Solo\nThis is your place, if you want to have a decent and fair priced Indian food. No fancy atmosphere, nothing special except food itself. I am a big fan of Indian cuisine, and all I tried here was tasty, no difference with what you would get in an average medium priced eatery somwhere in Delhi. Menu is limited and don't expect to get jeera rice for that money. But if you're in Saigon and miss Indian stuff, it's worth a visit, no doubt.\nRead more\nWritten January 31, 2016",
